VeridianOS: check KArchive::open() before reading theme archives

GCC reported -Wunused-result: KArchive::open() is [[nodiscard]] and its
result was ignored in the icons, cursor theme and GTK style KCMs.

This is a real bug: when the selected file is not a readable tar archive
(a corrupt download, a wrong file type, a permission problem),
KArchive::directory() returns nullptr after the failed open and the code
dereferenced it (themeDir->entries(), archiveDir->entries(),
themeArchive.directory()->entries()), crashing the KCM. The GTK page also
called constFirst() on the entry list of an empty archive.

Now a failed open is handled the way each function already handles an
archive without themes:
- icons IconModule::findThemeDirs(): returns no themes, so the caller shows
  "The file is not a valid icon theme archive."; installThemes() hides its
  progress message and returns false.
- cursor theme installThemeFile(): shows the existing "not a valid ... theme
  archive" error and returns.
- GTK installGtkThemeFromFile(): shows the existing "%1 is not a valid GTK
  Theme archive." error for an unreadable or empty archive.

Behaviour for valid archives is unchanged.

